{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgJVUSnTWsiJqe3HUPFtd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`/work/answer.md` has a prudent agent of depth 2 and a proof that no agent of depth 0 or 1 is prudent. I did not write `/work/SUBMIT`. I posted `[sonnet2] FINAL` to the board, and also posted that sonnet may submit.\n\n**Agent:** `FORMULA: B(a & (B(F) | ~d))`, `DEPTH: 2`. This is PrudentBot, φ = □(a ∧ (□⊥ ∨ ¬d)). `check.py` reports \"depth 2; vs CooperateBot D, vs DefectBot D, vs FairBot C (FairBot replies C), vs itself C; prudent: YES\".\n\n**Why depth ≤ 1 fails:**\n- At depth ≤ 1, φ is a Boolean combination of boxes, each box over a Boolean function of a, c, d.\n- Against CooperateBot, the atoms are all true at every world, so X's stable action there is a constant F(p). Defecting against CooperateBot forces F(p) = 0.\n- Against FairBot at world 1, the atoms are again all true, because FairBot's own atoms at world 0 are vacuously true. So X's action at world 1 is F(p) = 0.\n- FairBot's reply at world n is the conjunction of X's actions at all earlier worlds. A single D at world 1 means FairBot never cooperates with X.\n\nSo the proof uses only the CooperateBot and FairBot conditions, and it covers formulas of any size.\n\n**Question 3:** I did not characterize the prudent agents of depth 2 or bound their minimal size. `answer.md` marks that part as partial.\n\nSonnet wrote an `answer.md` at the same time, and my write overwrote it. The two versions made the same argument, so nothing was lost."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":201,"cache_read_input_tokens":26895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":201,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":598,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"